--- body ---
## Context

`experiments/derived/sota_cross_eval.csv` is listed as a prerequisite of
`exp2_mart.jsonl` in `experiments/analysis.mk` but has no rule to rebuild
it. Deleting the file causes `make` to fail with "no rule to make target".
The file was regenerated manually in PR #558 via a shell loop calling
`score_mechanical` 20 times (4 models × 5 runs, naive arm).

The correct fix is a `score-cross-eval` phony target (or a stamp-based
rule) that drives the loop from the Makefile, so `make` can reconstruct
the file without manual intervention.

## Relevant files

- `experiments/analysis.mk` — add the new rule here, near line 92 where
  `sota_cross_eval.csv` is consumed as a prerequisite
- `src/aedist/score_mechanical.py` — the per-row scorer CLI (`--arm`, `--model`, `--run`, `--naive-dir`, `--output-csv`)
- `experiments/derived/arm1_flat/` — the naive arm flat files; iterate
  `*.json` to discover model names and run numbers rather than hardcoding

## Actions

1. Add a `$(ANALYSIS_EXP2_CROSS_EVAL_CSV)` rule in `analysis.mk` that
   depends on `$(ANALYSIS_DERIVED_DIR)/arm1_flat/.done` and loops
   `score_mechanical` over all `arm1_flat/*.json` entries.
   Simplest form: a shell `for f in arm1_flat/*.json; do ...score_mechanical...; done`
   inside the recipe. Use `jq` or `python3 -c` to extract model/run from each JSON.
2. Remove the manual-loop instructions from any runbook/README that mentions them.
3. Wire `$(ANALYSIS_EXP2_CROSS_EVAL_CSV)` into `exp2-analysis` phony target
   if one exists, so `make exp2-analysis` drives a full rebuild end-to-end.

## Test

- Delete `experiments/derived/sota_cross_eval.csv` and run
  `make experiments/derived/sota_cross_eval.csv` (or `make exp2-analysis`).
- Verify 19–20 rows are produced with non-trivial precision (< 1.0).
- `make check-fast` passes.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make experiments/derived/sota_cross_eval.csv` rebuilds the file from scratch
- [ ] Rebuilt CSV has plausible precision values (not all 1.0)
- [ ] `make exp2-analysis` (or equivalent phony) drives the full pipeline end-to-end
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
